<title>USA: FDIC head Ricki Helfer to announce resignation - WSJ.</title>
<headline>FDIC head Ricki Helfer to announce resignation - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Federal Deposit Insurance Corp. chairman Ricki Helfer has told President Clinton she planned to resign by June, the Wall Street Journal said on Friday.</p>
<p>Helfer told the paper she would probably enter the private sector, although she would not be permitted to work in banking for two years after leaving the government regulatory agency.</p>
<p>&quot;I think I've accomplished what I set out to do here,&quot; she told the paper.</p>
</text>
